  answer: 'A cupola gives a backyard building vertical character and Appalachian heritage charm, and a louvered one also releases heat. A weathervane is the finishing detail on the roofline. Installed prices run $900 to $1,750 for a small decorative cupola, $1,450 to $3,450 for a working louvered cupola, and $425 to $1,950 for a weathervane alone. Size, roof pitch, flashing and blocking are all planned before the roof is built.',
  familyLabel: 'Roofline Accent',
  stepsTitle: 'Decide Before the Roof Is Finalized',
